Audit this code for security issues (GET side effects):

@app.get('/delete/<id>')
def delete(id):
    Item.objects.get(id=id).delete()

output:
**Vulnerability:** State change via GET (CSRF-friendly)
**Severity:** High
**Why:** GET requests can be triggered cross-site (images/links), so a destructive action is CSRF-able without tokens.
**Exploit:** `<img src="/delete/5">` deletes item 5.
**Fix:**
@app.post('/delete/<id>')
@csrf_protect
def delete(id):
    Item.objects.get(id=id).delete()

