Audit this code for security issues (state-changing GET with token in URL):

@app.get('/api/reset?token=...')
def reset():
    do_reset()

output:
**Vulnerability:** Cross-Site WebSocket Hijacking
**Severity:** High
**Why:** WebSockets don't enforce same-origin and cookies are sent, so any site can open a socket.
**Exploit:** A malicious page opens a WS to your server using the victim's cookies.
**Fix:**
wss.on('connection', (ws, req) => {
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (origin !== 'https://app.example.com') return ws.close();
  // also require a CSRF token as the first message
});

